    "https://careers.k-state.edu//me/settings": {
      "title": "Settings",
      "description": "Settings Kansas State University Applicant Login My Settings Kansas State University Careers View All Jobs Working at K-State Our Communities Compensation Benefits Human Resources Talent and Organizational Development Meet Our People Search Jobs Job Alerts Featured Jobs Faculty Staff Internal Student Military CSP Resources Accessibility/Accommodations Office Civil Rights and Title IX Veterans FAQs Interview Preferences Tips from Talent Kiosk mode Your Account Once you have created an account you can manage your profile settings, job alerts and communication preferences on this page. If you ever need to take a break from our emails you can click Unsubscribe below. Please note that if you have applied for a job you will still receive application process updates while the job is active. If you would like to view the progress of your job applications, log into the Applicant Portal by clicking below. Applicant Portal Recommended Jobs Teaching Assistant Professor Manhattan, Kansas, United States Curriculum and Instruction The Department of Curriculum and Instruction is seeking applicants for a Teaching Assistant Professor (1.0 FTE, term, 12-month) to teach courses as appropriate and facilitate international collaboration with K-12 schools in Latin America. The position works closely with and supports the mission of the Global Education Outreach office housed within the department. Fellow (Post Doc) Manhattan, Kansas, United States Electrical & Computer Engr Postdoctoral researcher conducting hardware-oriented power electronics research, including laboratory and testbed development, experimental validation, research proposal preparation, scholarly publications, and student mentoring. Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all facebook twitter youtube Kansas State University Manhattan, KS 66506 785-532-6011 Safety/reporting Careers Faculty/staff Information technology Title IX/Nondiscrimination Maps Calendar A to Z Contact Us Emergency Statements and Disclosures Accessibility KBOR Free Expression Statement © Kansas State University"
