    "https://careers.k-state.edu//our-communities": {
      "title": "Our Communities",
      "description": "Our Communities Kansas State University Applicant Login My Settings Kansas State University Careers View All Jobs Working at K-State Our Communities Compensation Benefits Human Resources Talent and Organizational Development Meet Our People Search Jobs Job Alerts Featured Jobs Faculty Staff Internal Student Military CSP Resources Accessibility/Accommodations Office Civil Rights and Title IX Veterans FAQs Interview Preferences Tips from Talent Kiosk mode Our Communities Manhattan | Olathe | Salina | Extension Manhattan K-State's main campus sits in \"The Little Apple,\" and thrives in its vibrant college-town atmosphere. Manhattan is a great atmosphere to explore new possibilities in a welcoming environment. In fact, the city was ranked one of the Top 10 college towns in the nation by the American Institute of Economic Research in 2017. Employees love Manhattan because it's big enough to offer opportunities and adventures but small enough to center on the university. Visit the Manhattan Area Chamber and Manhattan Convention and Visitors Bureau and learn how you are Made for Manhattan . Manhattan Jobs #9 \"Most Desirable\" place to live in the U.S. 12,500 Acres for outdoor lovers at Tuttle Creek Lake #1 Walkable Destination in Kansas One of the “Ten Best College Towns in America” Olathe Located within the Kansas Bioscience Park, the Olathe campus provides a direct portal linking the university's powerful research capabilities to the Greater Kansas City area and beyond. Olathe offers a unique blend of urban excitement and small-town charm. With a population exceeding 130,000, it is one of the fastest-growing cities in the U.S. and the fifth largest in Kansas. Despite its rapid growth, Olathe maintains a small town charm within a growing city, consistently ranked among the \"Best Cities\" to live by Money and Forbes magazines. Visit the Olathe Chamber of Commerce for more information on places to stay, shop and eat, as well as events and happenings around town! Olathe Jobs #4 Safest city in the United States (SmartAsset) 43 Neighborhood community parks #1 Greenest City in Kansas (Insurify) 200+ Dining options Salina This professional learning environment is built on theory, research, and industry application, all within a small campus atmosphere located in Salina, Kansas. Salina is a progressive city with a growing population of just under 50,000. Salina serves as the regional hub for state-of-the-art medical services, retail trade, and arts/entertainment. Salina is leading the way in the Midwest: from affordable housing and top-notch education to solid career opportunities and incredible arts and entertainment. Imagine the possibilities for you in Salina! Visit the Salina Chamber of Commerce for more information on places to stay, shop and eat, as well as events and happenings around town! Salina Jobs #2 Unmanned Aerial Systems College in the United States 50,000 Growing population 14.2 Minutes average commute time 17% Below the national average cost of living K-State is represented throughout Kansas K-State Extension K-State Extension provides research-based educational opportunities focused on improving the lives and communities of Kansans. Our network of specialists, agents, researchers and volunteers is present in each of the state's 105 counties.  As a land-grant institution, Kansas State University strives to connect community needs with university resources. We do this through a network of county, district, area and campus offices, agricultural experiment centers and sites. Find extension careers in any of our three main campuses or one of our partnering counties across Kansas. Relocating to Kansas MakeMyMove Kansas is a unique relocation marketplace that connects professionals with communities across the state offering financial incentives, local welcome packages, and personalized support to make moving easier and more rewarding. Through the program, eligible newcomers can access cash stipends, housing assistance, networking opportunities, and community perks designed to help you settle into your new Kansas home with confidence. Participating cities and regions offer a range of benefits tailored to newcomers, including job connections, experiences, and lifestyle incentives that showcase Kansas’s quality of life and strong community spirit. If relocating to Kansas, you can visit the site and apply online for program incentives; however, MakeMyMove applications must be submitted before receiving a job offer to be eligible for the program. Visit the MakeMyMove website to apply. #2 State for Cost of Living in the U.S. ( Forbes, 2023) #8 Friendliest State in America ( Big 7 Travel ) 122 Community Hospitals ( Kansas Hospital Association) #3 Best Place to Move to for Work (Onlineu, 2022) Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all facebook twitter youtube Kansas State University Manhattan, KS 66506 785-532-6011 Safety/reporting Careers Faculty/staff Information technology Title IX/Nondiscrimination Maps Calendar A to Z Contact Us Emergency Statements and Disclosures Accessibility KBOR Free Expression Statement © Kansas State University"
    },
