    "https://careers.k-state.edu//Featured-Jobs": {
      "title": "Featured Jobs",
      "description": "Featured Jobs Kansas State University Applicant Login My Settings Kansas State University Careers View All Jobs Working at K-State Our Communities Compensation Benefits Human Resources Talent and Organizational Development Meet Our People Search Jobs Job Alerts Featured Jobs Faculty Staff Internal Student Military CSP Resources Accessibility/Accommodations Office Civil Rights and Title IX Veterans FAQs Interview Preferences Tips from Talent Kiosk mode Featured Jobs Extension | IT | Custodial, Landscaping, Maintenance Extension K-State Extension improves Kansans' lives, livelihoods and communities through education, research, engagement and leadership. With educators in each of the state's 105 counties, our professionals strive to make the university's research and scientific accomplishments accessible and relevant to every household. Extension professionals provide research-based education and outreach in their communities, across the state, and around the world. Our state-wide team changes lives by solving problems and supporting communities through partnerships, innovation, and education. K-State Extension Featured Extension Job Openings: Title Worksite Location Department Employment Type Leavenworth Agriculture and Natural Resources Extension Agent On-site Other Ext Agents - Eastern Region Extension Agent / Educator Kearny County Extension Director On-site Other Ext Agents - Western Region Extension Agent / Educator Associate Director for Extension Field Operations On-site Manhattan 3670035010 Coop Extension Administration Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Sheridan County Extension Director On-site Other Ext Agents - North Region Extension Agent / Educator Decatur County Extension Director On-site Other Ext Agents - North Region Extension Agent / Educator People with Purpose: Nearly 300 miles from campus, Monica Walker carries Kansas State University with her every day. As a K-State Extension agent in Ulysses focused on family and community wellness and 4-H programming, Walker turns big ideas into everyday wins in her corner of Kansas — strengthening health, well-being and quality of life for Grant County and across the state. Read More Information Technology At Kansas State University, we understand the importance of a strong, secure and well-supported IT infrastructure in today’s global society. And as we align our people and resources to support our visionary Next-Gen K-State strategic plan , we are embarking on a transformative initiative that grows and bolsters our IT operations, enhancing how we strategically manage, support and align the university’s IT infrastructure across the institution. The Division of Information Technology at Kansas State University is dedicated to providing comprehensive technology solutions and support to enhance the academic, research, and administrative functions of the university. Our team delivers innovative IT services, ensuring seamless connectivity, robust cybersecurity, and cutting-edge digital tools that empower students, faculty, and staff. Learn more about our strategic hiring initiative here . Information Technology IT Jobs Featured IT Job Openings: Title Worksite Location Department Employment Type IT Support Specialist II On-site Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Asst Director, Information Technology On-site Manhattan Department of Housing & Dining Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Assistant Vice President of Research Technology On-site Manhattan Division of Info Tech Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Applications Developer I On-site Manhattan Research Vice President Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Enterprise Integration Developer On-site Manhattan Division of Info Tech Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Custodial, Landscaping, and Maintenance Join our Custodial, Landscaping, and Maintenance teams—essential contributors to the daily life of our university. Whether maintaining high-performance buildings, preserving beautiful green spaces, or ensuring vital systems work flawlessly, our Custodial, Landscaping, and Maintenance professionals form the backbone of campus operations. We’re seeking dedicated individuals—skilled in their craft, proud of their work, and committed to excellence. Explore roles in: Custodial Services – Help create a clean, healthy, and welcoming environment by performing routine and specialized cleaning in classrooms, offices, labs, and public spaces. Landscaping and Grounds – Enhance our campus environment with landscaping, irrigation, snow removal, and outdoor maintenance. Skilled Trades and Maintenance – Use your expertise as a carpenter, electrician, plumber, or technician to maintain infrastructure and support renovation projects. Support safe, efficient, and fully functional buildings through work in HVAC, electrical, plumbing, and general maintenance. Whether you're a seasoned tradesperson or ready to take the next step in your career, you'll find a welcoming team, strong benefits, and the chance to make a lasting difference every day. Custodial, Landscaping, and Maintenance Jobs Featured Custodial, Landscaping, and Maintenance Job Openings: Title Worksite Location Department Employment Type Facilities Maintenance Program Coordinator On-site Manhattan Fac Building Maintenance Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Maintenance and Repair Tech II On-site Manhattan Department of Housing & Dining Staff Full Time (USS) Custodial Specialist (Jardine Apts.) On-site Manhattan Department of Housing & Dining Staff Full Time (USS) Maintenance and Repair Tech II On-site Manhattan Fac Building Maintenance Staff Full Time (USS) Custodial Specialist On-site Manhattan Department of Housing & Dining Staff Full Time (USS) Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all facebook twitter youtube Kansas State University Manhattan, KS 66506 785-532-6011 Safety/reporting Careers Faculty/staff Information technology Title IX/Nondiscrimination Maps Calendar A to Z Contact Us Emergency Statements and Disclosures Accessibility KBOR Free Expression Statement © Kansas State University"
    },
