    "https://www.k-state.edu/careercenter/students/lets_go/handshake/": {
      "title": "Handshake",
      "description": "Handshake | K-State | Kansas State University Powercat chevron double-chevron chat-purple home computer window with a question mark close facebook linkedin menu search twitter youtube apply-purple apply-white chat-white request-purple request-white Jump to main content Jump to footer Kansas State University Canvas OrgCentral Navigate KSIS Time & Leave HRIS Webmail Sign in Browse A-Z Career Center Search Search K-State home Career Center Students Let's Go Handshake Join Handshake, the Career Center's recruiting and career services platform for K-State students, alumni and employers. Students and alumni can use Handshake to easily connect with employers, search for jobs and internships, review career fair/event information, and manage on-campus interviewing. Employers can use Handshake to identify qualified candidates for open positions, register for career fairs and manage on-campus recruitment activities. Undergrad and Graduate Students Enrolled undergraduate and graduate students can login to Handshake using your K-State eID and password. The Handshake phone app is available for Android and iPhones in the app store. Use the \"School Login\" button . Click on the icon for instructions on logging into the phone app. It is recommended to log in on a computer before using the app. New Admitted Students Admitted students can request a Handshake account to look for part-time jobs before coming to campus. Students will be uploaded into Handshake after class enrollment. We will not create an account more than a semester away from attendance. Employers Employers with a Handshake account can login using your email and Handshake password. Employers new to Handshake should create their account and connect with Kansas State University. K-State faculty and staff: please check out this important information about on-campus departments before creating your account. Alumni K-State graduates, prior to Aug 2017, who are job seeking are eligible to request a Handshake account through this alumni request form. For alumni, after Aug 2017, who lose their K-State email after two years, can request to have their account email changed to another email using this request. Please allow two business days for account login information to be sent. Please contact the Career Center if you need further assistance. Please review the Career Center's terms of use and the Handshake support page for more information. Career Center Berney Family Welcome Center 705 N. Martin Luther King Jr Drive, Manhattan, KS 66506-3412 785-532-6506 | careercenter@k-state.edu Hours of Operation Monday - Friday, 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. CT Chat is loading... Contact Us Emergency Statements and Disclosures Accessibility KBOR Free Expression Statement © Kansas State University Updated Updated: 8/18/26"
    },
    "https://careers.k-state.edu/career-skills-program/": {
      "title": "Military Career Skills Program",
      "description": "Career Skills Program Kansas State University Applicant Login My Settings Kansas State University Careers View All Jobs Working at K-State Our Communities Compensation Benefits Human Resources Talent and Organizational Development Meet Our People Search Jobs Job Alerts Featured Jobs Faculty Staff Internal Student Military CSP Resources Accessibility/Accommodations Office Civil Rights and Title IX Veterans FAQs Interview Preferences Tips from Talent Kiosk mode Military Career Skills Program K-State is honored to offer Career Skills Program and DOD Skillbridge internship opportunities for transitioning service members. Our internships are designed to help you acquire valuable skills in the field of higher education, providing a seamless transition from military to civilian life. These opportunities span roles such as HR Representatives, IT Support Specialists, Risk and Compliance Assistants, and Paralegals—helping you translate your military experience into in-demand civilian careers. At K-State, we are deeply committed to supporting your employment preparedness with comprehensive on-the-job training, interview preparation, networking opportunities, and personalized feedback on your resume. By participating in a CSP or DoD Skillbridge internship at K-State, you will have the unique opportunity to apply your military knowledge and abilities in a dynamic educational environment. You'll contribute meaningfully to K-State’s mission while growing and refining your skills in new and exciting ways. Our supportive community and dedicated staff are here to ensure that you gain the confidence and competence needed for a successful civilian career. Apply Now for a Career Skills Internship My experience as an intern for K-State was a great experience.  It helped me gain experience in the civilian sector of my career field while building relationships and networking with others. It also helped ease the transition from the Military to the civilian side of the work force.\" David Alsup Career Skills Program Information DOD SkillBridge Program Information FAQ Career Skills Program Can K-State provide CSP and DoD Skillbridge internships? Yes, K-State can provide CSP and DoD Skillbridge internships under the KansasWorks MOU umbrella. What is the process to secure a CSP/DoD SkillBridge internship at K-State? First, please fill out an expression of interest application. Upon submission of your materials K-State HR will review your application and send it to departments that may be a match for your skills, interests, and timeline. K-State HR or a hiring manager will reach out to you if there is a match. You may be invited to an informal or formal interview with the hiring manager to determine your eligibility for the position in which you are interested. Please provide your department with any necessary documentation. What types of internships are available? K-State has a variety of departments across our campus each with diverse jobs in different areas of expertise. We will try to match you with an internship that suits your skills and interests. Areas of interest include: Business, accounting, and finance Communications and marketing Facilities, grounds, and skilled trades Health and safety Student affairs and services Administrative and professional Information Technology Human resources What happens when my internship is over? When your internship is over, your hiring manager and you will discuss if a permanent position is available for you. If no position is available, K-State HR will work with you to provide resources for other positions available at K-State that you may qualify for. From there you would apply for the position and go through the standard hiring process. Have Questions? Complete the form below and a member of the talent acquisition team will contact you. First Name (required) 0de7ecdc Last Name (required) 8e71b926 Email (required) ef4284ee Are you interested in a specific position/job? 48bc6b4f Question for the K-State Talent Acquisition Team (required) 144607f5 I agree to be contacted about career opportunities at K-State via email, mobile text, and phone (if applicable). (required) a393eda7 Reach Out! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) 7ae5a7fd Last Name (required) 7317fc76 Email (required) 1c17f4b5 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all facebook twitter youtube Kansas State University Manhattan, KS 66506 785-532-6011 Safety/reporting Careers Faculty/staff Information technology Title IX/Nondiscrimination Maps Calendar A to Z Contact Us Emergency Statements and Disclosures Accessibility KBOR Free Expression Statement © Kansas State University"
    },
    "https://careers.k-state.edu//FAQs": {
      "title": "Frequently Asked Questions and Resources",
      "description": "FAQs Kansas State University Applicant Login My Settings Kansas State University Careers View All Jobs Working at K-State Our Communities Compensation Benefits Human Resources Talent and Organizational Development Meet Our People Search Jobs Job Alerts Featured Jobs Faculty Staff Internal Student Military CSP Resources Accessibility/Accommodations Office Civil Rights and Title IX Veterans FAQs Interview Preferences Tips from Talent Kiosk mode Frequently Asked Questions and Resources Frequently Asked Questions What is it like to work at K-State? Join our talent network and find out. We will send information to help you: Stay updated on all things K-State employment Access resources for the hiring process Know about any upcoming hiring events Can I apply for multiple positions at K-State? Yes. You may apply to multiple positions and manage your applications under one applicant account. Can I update my application materials after I submit my application? Yes and no. You may make updates to your personal information and upload a revised resume, cover letter or other attachment at any time through your applicant account. However, you are unable to make changes to job-specific application questions once your application is submitted. How do I know if the job I’m interested in is accepting applications? All posted jobs are open and accepting applications.  We work diligently to keep all postings updated throughout the recruitment process. When will I hear back about my application? You can check the status of your application in your applicant portal by clicking on Applicant Login at the top of the page.  You will hear directly from the department or search committee regarding any next steps in the application process. I don’t see a position of interest. Can I set up an alert for specific roles I’m interested in? If you are interested in working at K-State but do not see a job currently posted relevant to your skills and experience, you can sign up for Job Alerts to receive updates based on your criteria. I'm not ready to apply. Can I save a job and apply later? Yes, you can send a job to yourself or add it to your favorites and view it in \"my settings\" at the top of the screen. Apply when you're ready. I would like some assistance to complete my application.  Is there someone who can help me? We’d love to help.  Email or call us at KStateCareers@k-state.edu or (785) 532-6255.  If you need access to a computer, you can also stop by our Human Resources office during business hours and use our available computer. I need an accommodation for the interview or application process.  Is there someone who can assist me? Yes! Our Accommodations Specialist, Emily Everts, will be happy to assist you.  You may contact her directly at eeverts@k-state.edu or (785) 532-1908. I don’t remember my password to login to my applicant account.  What should I do? There are multiple ways to login. Click on Applicant Login at the top of our page and enter your email address.  From there you’ll see the various ways to login or reset your password. I don't have a degree, can I still apply at K-State? K-State recognizes the value of both education and experience in setting minimum qualifications for staff jobs. To learn more, visit our qualifications and equivalencies for staff roles website page. What is the difference between USS and Unclassified positions? At Kansas State University there are two different employment types: Unclassified Professional Staff (UNC) and University Support Staff (USS). Unclassified Professional Staff are generally faculty, administrators, and other professional staff. University Support Staff (USS) generally include our technical and service staff along with some professional and clerical staff. There are many similarities and differences between these two employment types, which are detailed on our website . What is the difference between a regular position and a term position? Term positions have a specified end date or specific funding that is finite.  Term positions may be renewed.  Regular positions do not have specified end dates or finite funding. Does K-State have any hybrid or remote work options? Yes, some positions offer remote or hybrid work options.  Filter by Worksite on our job search page to find the positions that are remote or hybrid eligible.  Additional details of hybrid arrangements can be found in the position announcements.  An employee who is working remotely for K-State must reside within the United States in order to comply with all federal and state laws, filings, or tax requirements. Remote and hybrid work arrangements are not available for anyone who resides in the state of Idaho. I accepted my offer online. Can I have a copy of that offer letter or contract? Yes, you can access your offer documents from the \"view application\" button next to the position in your applicant account.  If you are unable to find it, please contact us at KStateCareers@k-state.edu . Applicant Resources: Accessibility Employee Resource Groups Veterans Contact a Recruiter Thank you for your interest in K-State! Complete the form below and a member of the talent acquisition team will contact you. First Name (required) 11c66ced Last Name (required) 97718b3b Email (required) b5dd40c3 Are you interested in a specific position/job? a2edbca0 Question for the K-State Talent Acquisition Team (required) f05d101d I agree to be contacted about career opportunities at K-State via email, mobile text, and phone (if applicable). (required) 609bb56e Reach Out! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Register below to join our talent network First Name (required) c1fae7bf Last Name (required) 5e8ddeaa Email (required) de637219 Join Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all facebook twitter youtube Kansas State University Manhattan, KS 66506 785-532-6011 Safety/reporting Careers Faculty/staff Information technology Title IX/Nondiscrimination Maps Calendar A to Z Contact Us Emergency Statements and Disclosures Accessibility KBOR Free Expression Statement © Kansas State University"
    },
    "https://careers.k-state.edu/interview-preferences": {
      "title": "Interview Preferences",
      "description": "Interview Preferences Kansas State University Applicant Login My Settings Kansas State University Careers View All Jobs Working at K-State Our Communities Compensation Benefits Human Resources Talent and Organizational Development Meet Our People Search Jobs Job Alerts Featured Jobs Faculty Staff Internal Student Military CSP Resources Accessibility/Accommodations Office Civil Rights and Title IX Veterans FAQs Interview Preferences Tips from Talent Kiosk mode Interview Preferences Veterans Preference Kansas State University is committed to recognizing the sacrifices made by those serving in the Armed Forces by fully recognizing and honoring the State of Kansas Veterans Preference, the Uniformed Services Employment and Reemployment Rights Act (USERRA), and the Vietnam Era Veterans Readjustment Assistance Act (VEVRAA). Any person wishing to be considered eligible for a Veterans preference must submit a fully completed DD-214 or NGB-22 form for the Veteran service member along with other application materials when applying for a position. Documentation will remain confidential and only be used to verify eligibility for the preference. Documentation must be submitted by the closing date noted on the position announcement. If they meet the minimum qualifications of the position and submit all required application materials, they will receive a first-level interview for the position. The preference does not guarantee that an applicant will be hired, as positions are filled with the best qualified candidate as determined by the hiring manager. A person who wishes to utilize the preference will submit a copy of their DD-214 or NGB-22 along with their application materials.  Kansas State Law – K.S.A. 73-201 provides veterans preference for veterans who separated honorably from the armed forces under honorable conditions. Disability Preference Applicants who have physical, cognitive and/or mental disabilities may claim an interview preference when applying for certain eligible positions. If the applicant meets the minimum qualifications for the position, can perform the essential functions of the position, with or without reasonable accommodation(s), submits qualifying documentation, and submits all required application materials, they will receive a first-level interview for the position. The disability interview preference does not guarantee that an applicant will be hired, as positions are filled with the best qualified candidate as determined by the hiring manager. To qualify for this disability interview preference, applicants must complete the disability interview preference request form and include appropriate documentation. Documentation must be submitted by the closing date noted on the position announcement. Eligible documentation includes: Supplemental security income or social security disability insurance determination letter Letter from a managed care organization or a qualified medical professional attesting to the disability Home and community-based services waiver approval letter Vocational rehabilitation letter from a vocational rehabilitation counselor Any person wishing to request this interview preference will only need to submit documentation one time. If verified, they will be eligible for the disability interview preference for all future applications for eligible positions. Requesting an Interview Preference To request an interview preference, follow the steps in the application form.  If you already submitted an application for a qualifying position and you would like to request an interview preference, please email KStateCareers@k-state.edu. If the position is still open and accepting applications as noted by the closing date on the job advertisement, and your application is still in search committee review as noted in your PageUp applicant account, an additional information form with instructions will be sent to you. The additional information form and all supporting documentation must be submitted by the closing date on the job advertisement. Exclusions Kansas State University honors interview preferences for qualified applicants who are veterans or individuals with disabilities. Eligible applicants who meet the minimum qualifications, submit all required application materials, and submit required preference documentation will be granted a first-level interview. The disability and veteran interview preferences do not apply to student employment positions, temporary positions, athletics positions, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all facebook twitter youtube Kansas State University Manhattan, KS 66506 785-532-6011 Safety/reporting Careers Faculty/staff Information technology Title IX/Nondiscrimination Maps Calendar A to Z Contact Us Emergency Statements and Disclosures Accessibility KBOR Free Expression Statement © Kansas State University"
    },
    "https://careers.k-state.edu//tips-from-talent": {
      "title": "Hiring Process and Tips",
      "description": "Tips From Talent Kansas State University Applicant Login My Settings Kansas State University Careers View All Jobs Working at K-State Our Communities Compensation Benefits Human Resources Talent and Organizational Development Meet Our People Search Jobs Job Alerts Featured Jobs Faculty Staff Internal Student Military CSP Resources Accessibility/Accommodations Office Civil Rights and Title IX Veterans FAQs Interview Preferences Tips from Talent Kiosk mode Hiring Process and Tips Hiring Process Preparation: Polish your resume, craft a compelling cover letter, and gather references to ensure your documents shine. Application: Submit your resume, cover letter, and any other required documents through K-State’s online portal. Double-check for accuracy and be sure to complete all application questions. Screening: The hiring committee reviews applications and contacts selected candidates for initial interviews.  Your application status can be viewed on your applicant profile.  You will receive a notification when your application status changes. Interview: Impress in virtual interviews or in-person meetings with the team. Be ready to showcase your skills and enthusiasm. Offer and Background Check: Celebrate receiving a verbal and then a written offer!  Once our offer has been accepted complete a background check and any other pre-employment requirements.  Official written offers are sent via email and background checks are authorized electronically. Onboarding: Lock in your start date, finish all paperwork, and enjoy orientation. Meet your new team, learn about university policies, benefits, and job-specific training. Engage and integrate smoothly into your new role. Tips from our Talent Acquisition Team Application Tailor your resume to the position for which you are applying. Quantify your success. Numbers speak volumes. Include specific achievements and quantify them whenever possible. e.g., increased sales by 20%, managed a team of 10. Follow instructions during the application process: Read the application instructions carefully. Missing a step can disqualify you from consideration. Upload your resume and allow our system to fill in the application fields. Please note that the document format can impact how the fields import.  You may still have to complete or correct some fields. Give your references a heads up! Contact a list of professional references who are able and ready to speak to your qualifications and work ethic. Ensure that your email address and phone number are accurate as we communicate frequently by email and phone. Interview Prepare for interviews, don’t try to wing it. Prepare answers for common interview questions and behavioral questions using the STAR method (Situation, Task, Action, Result). Review the job posting and requirements for the position before your interview. Practice talking about your knowledge, skills, and abilities and how they apply to the role. Ensure you have the appropriate Zoom link, address of interview, and other pertinent information ahead of time so you are prepared on the day of the interview. Ask your search committee questions. This shows you have a vested interest in the University and have thought about being successful in the role. Send a thank you email to the search committee members after the interview. Offer and Onboarding Be sure to complete all new hire paperwork and to authorize your background check, if applicable. Check your email daily. You may receive email reminders of tasks to be completed, which could impact the timely processing of your first paycheck. Take note of when and where you should arrive on your first day of work. Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all facebook twitter youtube Kansas State University Manhattan, KS 66506 785-532-6011 Safety/reporting Careers Faculty/staff Information technology Title IX/Nondiscrimination Maps Calendar A to Z Contact Us Emergency Statements and Disclosures Accessibility KBOR Free Expression Statement © Kansas State University"
    },
    "https://www.k-state.edu/hr/careers/executive-profile/": {
      "title": "University Executive Profile",
      "description": "Kansas State University Profile Powercat chevron double-chevron chat-purple home computer window with a question mark close facebook linkedin menu search twitter youtube apply-purple apply-white chat-white request-purple request-white Jump to main content Jump to footer Kansas State University Canvas OrgCentral Navigate KSIS Time & Leave HRIS Webmail Sign in Browse A-Z Human Resources Search Search University Executive Profile K-State home Human Resources Executive Profile Explore Kansas State University Kansas State University (K-State) seeks experienced, accomplished and authentic leaders with a strong commitment to our institution's land-grant mission, vision and values. University Overview, Mission and Vision University and Student Achievements University Values About Manhattan, Kansas K-State Athletics Strategic Planning Research, Scholarship, Creative Activities and Discovery Facilities Contact Us Emergency Statements and Disclosures Accessibility KBOR Free Expression Statement © Kansas State University Updated Updated: 10/14/25"
    },
    "https://www.facebook.com/KStateCareers": {
      "title": "Facebook",
      "description": "Facebook Facebook Log In Log In Forgot Account? This content isn't available right now When this happens, it's usually because the owner only shared it with\n        a small group of people, changed who can see it or it's been deleted. Go to Feed Go back Visit Help Center"
